   "source": [
    "# GP2.1 NPEC - Guest Practicum - Tomato Dataset"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "74afc527",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "```console\n",
    "███╗   ██╗██████╗ ███████╗ ██████╗\n",
    "████╗  ██║██╔══██╗██╔════╝██╔════╝\n",
    "██╔██╗ ██║██████╔╝█████╗  ██║     \n",
    "██║╚██╗██║██╔═══╝ ██╔══╝  ██║     \n",
    "██║ ╚████║██║     ███████╗╚██████╗\n",
    "╚═╝  ╚═══╝╚═╝     ╚══════╝ ╚═════╝\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "75b78c3c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "252 tomato plants, 4 soil treatments (`Mock`, `PGPR_1`, `PGPR_2`, `PGPR_3`), infected with a leaf pathogen or not, after 10 days of growth. Three NPEC sensors recorded daily: chlorophyll fluorescence (**FC1**), hyperspectral reflectance (**VNIR**), 3D scanning (**S3D**).\n",
    "\n",
    "Fill in the 2 functions marked `# TODO your code here`, then answer the short questions (e.g. **Q1.**)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "426056ec",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Load the data"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "0847ce98",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-09-22T23:05:03.042116Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-09-22T23:05:03.042116Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-09-22T23:05:04.745065Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-09-22T23:05:04.745065Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "from sklearn.decomposition import PCA\n",
    "from sklearn.impute import SimpleImputer\n",
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.style.use(\"seaborn-v0_8-whitegrid\")\n",
    "plt.rcParams[\"figure.dpi\"] = 150\n",
    "RANDOM_STATE = 42\n",
    "\n",
    "TREATMENT_ORDER = [\"Mock\", \"PGPR_1\", \"PGPR_2\", \"PGPR_3\"]\n",
    "TREATMENT_STYLE = {\n",
    "    \"Mock\":   {\"color\": \"#2a78d6\", \"marker\": \"o\"},\n",
    "    \"PGPR_1\": {\"color\": \"#eb6834\", \"marker\": \"s\"},\n",
    "    \"PGPR_2\": {\"color\": \"#1baf7a\", \"marker\": \"^\"},\n",
    "    \"PGPR_3\": {\"color\": \"#4a3aa7\", \"marker\": \"D\"},\n",
    "}\n",
    "INFECTION_STYLE = {\n",
    "    \"Healthy\":  {\"color\": \"#2a78d6\", \"marker\": \"o\"},\n",
    "    \"Infected\": {\"color\": \"#d03b3b\", \"marker\": \"s\"},\n",
    "}\n",
    "PHASE_STYLE = {\n",
    "    \"P1\": {\"color\": \"#2a78d6\", \"marker\": \"o\"},   # growth, before infection\n",
    "    \"P2\": {\"color\": \"#eb6834\", \"marker\": \"s\"},   # after infection\n",
    "}\n",
    "AREA_ORDER = [\"A4\", \"B2\", \"C4\", \"D2\"]   # the 4 positions in a tray\n",
    "AREA_COLORS = dict(zip(AREA_ORDER, [\"#9ec5f4\", \"#3987e5\", \"#1c5cab\", \"#0d366b\"]))\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def scatter_by_group(ax, coordinates, groups, style, title):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Draw one 2D scatter, coloring and marking each group consistently.\"\"\"\n",
    "    for name, spec in style.items():\n",
    "        mask = groups == name\n",
    "        if not mask.any():\n",
    "            continue\n",
    "        ax.scatter(\n",
    "            coordinates[mask, 0], coordinates[mask, 1],\n",
    "            c=spec[\"color\"], marker=spec[\"marker\"], s=6, alpha=0.35,\n",
    "            linewidths=0, label=name,\n",
    "        )\n",
    "    ax.set_title(title, fontsize=10)\n",
    "    ax.set_xticks([]); ax.set_yticks([]); ax.grid(False)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2e11e8d1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "One table: one row per plant per day, both phases. 10 of ~60 recorded traits, one per column. `Tray`/`Area` mark each plant's spot in its tray.\n",
    "\n",
    "| trait | sensor | what it measures |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| `QY_Lss` | FC1 (fluorescence) | Effective PSII quantum yield, steady-state light-adapted (`Fq_Lss / Fm_Lss`) — photosynthetic efficiency; typically drops under stress. |\n",
    "| `FvFm_Lss` | FC1 | Maximum PSII quantum efficiency, steady-state light-adapted (`Fv_Lss / Fm_Lss`) — a classic photosynthetic-stress indicator. |\n",
    "| `FC1_Size` | FC1 | Number of pixels in the plant mask used for the fluorescence calculation — a size proxy from the fluorescence camera. |\n",
    "| `NDVI_avg` | VNIR (hyperspectral) | Normalized Difference Vegetation Index, `(R800-R670)/(R800+R670)` — canopy greenness / vigor. |\n",
    "| `PRI_avg` | VNIR | Photochemical Reflectance Index, `(R531-R570)/(R531+R570)` — sensitive to xanthophyll-cycle (light-use efficiency) changes. |\n",
    "| `SIPI_avg` | VNIR | A pigment-reflectance index, `(R790-R450)/(R790+R650)` — sensitive to pigment composition and senescence. |\n",
    "| `VNIR_Size` | VNIR | The hyperspectral analyzer's own size measurement — a size proxy from the reflectance camera. |\n",
    "| `PlantHeight` | S3D (3D) | Vertical extent of the plant's 3D point cloud, `max(Z) - min(Z)`. |\n",
    "| `NumPoints` | S3D | Number of points in the processed 3D point cloud — a size/density proxy. |\n",
    "| `HullVolume` | S3D | Volume enclosed by the convex hull of the 3D point cloud — an overall plant-volume proxy. |"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "2d5ccf29",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-09-22T23:05:04.747078Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-09-22T23:05:04.747078Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-09-22T23:05:04.779133Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-09-22T23:05:04.779133Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "TRAIT_NAMES = [\"QY_Lss\", \"FvFm_Lss\", \"FC1_Size\", \"NDVI_avg\", \"PRI_avg\",\n",
    "               \"SIPI_avg\", \"VNIR_Size\", \"PlantHeight\", \"NumPoints\", \"HullVolume\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def load_tomato_dataset(path):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Load and validate the long-format trait table (one row per plant per day).\"\"\"\n",
    "    frame = pd.read_csv(path)\n",
    "    expected = [\"Plant_ID\", \"Tray\", \"Area\", \"Treatment\", \"Infection\", \"Phase\", \"day\"] + TRAIT_NAMES\n",
    "    assert list(frame.columns) == expected\n",
    "    assert frame[\"Plant_ID\"].nunique() == 252\n",
    "    assert set(frame[\"Treatment\"]) == set(TREATMENT_ORDER)\n",
    "    assert set(frame[\"Infection\"]) == set(INFECTION_STYLE)\n",
    "    assert set(frame[\"Phase\"]) == set(PHASE_STYLE)\n",
    "    return frame\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# OFFLINE: \n",
    "# tomato = load_tomato_dataset(\"tomato_traits.csv\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# ONLINE:\n",
    "tomato = load_tomato_dataset(\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/SinitcynLab/INFOMQUDA/main/assignments/module2/tomato_traits.csv\")\n",
    "print(f\"{len(tomato)} rows, {tomato.Plant_ID.nunique()} plants\")\n",
    "tomato.head(3)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "23676805",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. A first look: plant height over time\n",
    "\n",
    "S3D gives plant height directly, in centimeters - easiest trait to picture.\n",
    "Average height per day by tray position (`Area`): columns are Phase 1 (growth) / Phase 2 (infection), rows are eventually-healthy vs eventually-infected plants."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "847a6d7c",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-09-22T23:05:04.781143Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-09-22T23:05:04.781143Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-09-22T23:05:05.430849Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-09-22T23:05:05.430849Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(2, 2, figsize=(9, 6.4), sharex=\"col\", sharey=\"col\")\n",
    "columns = [(\"P1\", \"Phase 1: growth\"), (\"P2\", \"Phase 2: infection\")]\n",
    "for row, infection in enumerate([\"Healthy\", \"Infected\"]):\n",
    "    for col, (phase, title) in enumerate(columns):\n",
    "        ax = axes[row, col]\n",
    "        subset = tomato[(tomato.Phase == phase) & (tomato.Infection == infection)]\n",
    "        for area in AREA_ORDER:\n",
    "            grp = subset[subset.Area == area].groupby("day")["PlantHeight"]\n",
    "            mean, lo, hi = grp.mean(), grp.quantile(0.25), grp.quantile(0.75)\n",
    "            ax.fill_between(mean.index, lo.values, hi.values, color=AREA_COLORS[area], alpha=0.15, linewidth=0)\n",
    "            ax.plot(mean.index, mean.values, marker="o", ms=3, color=AREA_COLORS[area], label=area)\n",
    "        if row == 0:\n",
    "            ax.set_title(title, fontsize=10)\n",
    "        if col == 0:\n",
    "            ax.set_ylabel(f\"{infection}\\nPlantHeight\")\n",
    "axes[1, 0].set_xlabel(\"day\")\n",
    "axes[1, 1].set_xlabel(\"day\")\n",
    "axes[0, 0].legend(fontsize=7, frameon=False, title=\"tray position\")\n",
    "fig.tight_layout()"
   ]
  },
