  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "efea3e3e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Missing values: MCAR, MAR, or MNAR?\n",
    "\n",
    "Three ways data can go missing:\n",
    "- **MCAR**- missing completely at random, unrelated to any value\n",
    "- **MAR** - missingness predictable from other *observed* columns\n",
    "- **MNAR** - missingness depends on the value that's missing itself\n",
    "\n",
    "`VNIR` is essentially complete; `FC1` and `S3D` each miss ~6-7% - same size gap, different cause."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "0d1188f8",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-09-22T23:05:05.434364Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-09-22T23:05:05.432855Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-09-22T23:05:05.441893Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-09-22T23:05:05.441385Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "tomato[TRAIT_NAMES].isna().mean().sort_values(ascending=False)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "8b3a9c72",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-09-22T23:05:05.444403Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-09-22T23:05:05.444403Z",
